# The variables of this project: everything the compose files read, plus IBERGRID_DOMAIN, which
# is reserved for phase 6. For local development run `make env`, which writes a .env with random
# values for the required secrets; the rest have working defaults.
# The repository is public: .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.

# --- Object storage (S3 API) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Local: the RustFS root keys (any random strings). Production: the access key ID and
# secret of a Cloudflare R2 API token scoped to the bucket.
# Rotating them: the catalog keeps its own copy of the pair, stored in the warehouse when
# catalog-init created it, and bootstrap never updates an existing warehouse. After changing them
# here, push the new pair to the catalog (it calls POST /management/v1/warehouse/{id}/storage
# with the credential and the warehouse's profile, where only the fields ibergrid owns are reset:
# flavor, endpoint, region, path-style, remote signing; Lakekeeper validates it before saving):
#   local:  make up && docker compose run --rm --no-deps catalog-init catalog update-credential
#   server: docker compose --env-file .env --env-file release.env -f compose.yaml \
#             -f compose.prod.yaml run --rm --no-deps catalog-init catalog update-credential
# The same command turns remote signing off on a warehouse created before ADR 0002 (locally,
# `make down-volumes && make up` recreates the warehouse instead).
IBERGRID_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
IBERGRID_S3_SECRET_KEY=
# Production only (required there): https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# Local default: http://storage:9000 (the RustFS container).
#IBERGRID_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=
# Local default us-east-1; production default auto (what R2 expects).
#IBERGRID_S3_REGION=
#IBERGRID_S3_BUCKET=ibergrid

# --- Catalog: Lakekeeper on Postgres -----------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Password of the lakekeeper Postgres role. URL-safe characters only: it is embedded
# in a postgresql:// connection URL.
LAKEKEEPER_DB_PASSWORD=
# Required. Encrypts the storage credentials Lakekeeper keeps in Postgres. Changing or losing it
# makes the stored credentials unreadable, so keep it with the database backups.
LAKEKEEPER_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# Name of the Iceberg warehouse (also its key prefix inside the bucket).
#IBERGRID_CATALOG_WAREHOUSE=lakehouse

# --- Orchestration: Dagster on Postgres (ADR 0005) ----------------------------------------------
# Required. Password of the dagster Postgres role (run, event and schedule storage). URL-safe
# characters only.
DAGSTER_DB_PASSWORD=
# The schedules (REData daily, OMIE twice a day, the audit-branch sweeper) start stopped, so a
# local stack never calls the sources on its own; production defaults to true. Each can also be
# started in the UI (http://127.0.0.1:28300).
#IBERGRID_ORCHESTRATION_SCHEDULES_RUNNING=false

# --- Sources: Red Eléctrica REData (public API, no token) ---------------------------------------
# Defaults below. One ingestion process never sends more than one request a second (MAX_RPS is
# capped at 1; the limit is per process, so N parallel processes send up to N a second) and
# retries timeouts, 429 and 5xx a few times; a whole year of national daily generation took 19 s
# to answer, hence the generous timeout (seconds per request).
#IBERGRID_REDATA_BASE_URL=https://apidatos.ree.es
#IBERGRID_REDATA_TIMEOUT=60
#IBERGRID_REDATA_MAX_RPS=1

# --- Sources: OMIE day-ahead market files (public downloads, no token) --------------------------
# Defaults below. One file per delivery day, at most one request a second per process (capped at
# 1), with the same retries as REData; a day's file is about 2.7 KB.
#IBERGRID_OMIE_BASE_URL=https://www.omie.es
#IBERGRID_OMIE_TIMEOUT=30
#IBERGRID_OMIE_MAX_RPS=1

# --- Logging -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR. Containers always log JSON.
#IBERGRID_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- Production only (compose.prod.yaml, on the server) ----------------------------------------
# Image repositories on GHCR (defaults below), run by the digests in release.env. The deploy job
# (deploy/remote.sh) writes IBERGRID_APP_DIGEST and IBERGRID_ORCHESTRATION_DIGEST
# (sha256:<64 hex>) to release.env on every release; do not set them here.
#IBERGRID_IMAGE=ghcr.io/jaisato/ibergrid-lakehouse
#IBERGRID_ORCHESTRATION_IMAGE=ghcr.io/jaisato/ibergrid-lakehouse-orchestration
# Reserved for the public endpoints of phase 6: not read by anything yet.
#IBERGRID_DOMAIN=ibergrid-lakehouse.jasato.com
